  "body": "Stacked on #4482 - do not merge before #4482.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New command `RenameTool { from, to }` (`crates/app/src/commands/tool_rename.rs`). It sets the new `Name` on the tool entity and the `tool` field of each operation that uses the tool. This is one undo step. The entity stays, so the tool keeps its definition, number, holder body, drawn cutter and component stack.\n- A name is not an input of a toolpath. An operation that is Ok before the rename gets its stamp again, so it stays Ok. A Stale operation stays Stale.\n- `RenameTool::new` refuses by name, before the history:\n  - an empty name (after a trim) or a control character;\n  - an unknown name, or an entity that is not a tool;\n  - the same name;\n  - a name that another entity has, or that a setup reserves;\n  - a name that an operation still names (the operation of a deleted tool must not take this tool);\n  - a name that the machine reserves (`tool_reservations::for_tool_as`).\n- New MCP tool `rename_tool { name, new_name }` (`crates/app/src/mcp/tool_rename.rs`). It runs the same command. The rows in `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and in the site guide are added.\n- The Name row of the tool library editor is a text field (`tool_tab.rs`). The typed name is a draft of the window (`ToolLibraryView::rename`). Apply queues `RenameTool` after the other draft commands. A typed name makes the draft dirty, so Duplicate (#4482) waits for Apply. Cancel drops the typed name. A refused name keeps the typed text.\n- The views follow a renamed tool (`crates/ui/src/state_tool_rename.rs`, called once in `drain_actions`): the library editor, the Properties target and draft, and the tool shape window. A view follows only when it still shows the old name that was recorded before the commands of the frame ran, and the same entity now has a new name. Thus a view that moved to another tool (Duplicate opens the copy) stays, and a rename of another tool does not move it. This covers Apply, undo, redo and an agent's `rename_tool` (the MCP host runs inside `drain_actions`).\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/4370-rename-tool.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/rename_tool.rs` (in the existing `tool_library_holders` suite, no new test binary):\n  - `rename_moves_the_tool_and_its_operation_in_one_undo_step`\n  - `a_stale_operation_stays_stale_through_a_rename`\n  - `rename_refuses_by_name_and_changes_nothing`\n  - `mcp_rename_tool_runs_the_command_and_undo_restores_it`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_rename.rs` (a module of the `camcraft-ui` lib tests):\n  - `the_name_row_is_a_text_field_and_typing_is_a_draft`\n  - `apply_renames_the_tool_and_its_operations_in_one_undo_step`\n  - `a_rename_of_another_tool_leaves_the_open_editor_alone` (Duplicate, then a rename of the copy, its undo and its redo: the editor stays on its tool)\n  - `an_empty_name_is_refused_and_cancel_drops_the_typed_name`\n- `layout_window_tool_editor` asserts the Name text field.\n- The existing `tool_library_frame::duplicate_opens_the_copy_and_is_one_undo_step` stays green: the follow law does not pull the editor back from the copy.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 2021 on the parent head 6189d81, 2025 on this head.\n\nGate on the final head b7878b42547eeb9c37667fcca4e183229a922d78 (lanes, log `gate-4370-b7878b425.log`):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 394 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (43.0 min). One SKIP: `site tests` (the lane has no `zola`); this is not a pass for the site guide row\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (exit 0)\n\nThe base of the quick gate is `origin/main`, so the plan also covers the commits of #4482.\n\nNo post, toolpath or geometry changed, so no example catalog suite and no light lane step applies. This is a `P7` PR, so no heavy step.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A rename from a live MCP client against a running window. The ui test drives the same `CommandKind::RenameTool` path, and the MCP host runs inside `drain_actions`.\n- The cut recipe library, machine reservation files and exported `.camtools` files keep the old name. They are outside the document. A recipe that names the old tool is refused by name when it is used (see the decision file).\n- Unapplied field edits in the library editor are read again from the tool when an undo or an agent renames the open tool.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe draw code of the editor did not change after these renders.\n\nBefore (the Name row is a label):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4510/before.png)\n\nAfter (the Name row is a text field with a typed new name):\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4510/after.png)\n\nChangelog: Tool library: the tool editor can rename a tool. Each operation that uses the tool follows the new name in the same undo step. The MCP tool `rename_tool` does the same for agents.\n\nEffort: max (escalated from high after two red quick gates; this head has the fixes and a new pin for the follow law)\n\nFixes #4370\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
